# What the e2 motif-supplement rules produce, in sha256sum format, paths relative to
# data/derived. e2_fig_supp_motif_verify checks a build against it.
#
# The three JSON caches are plain data and match on any host with E2's deposit: they read
# the deposit, the motif set files and nothing else. Two things they deliberately do NOT
# depend on, each of which moved a digest here while every number in the file stayed as it
# was. The finished table is digested PARSED rather than as a file, over the rows these
# steps read -- the complete and retired ones -- and by the round file's BASENAME: the
# table carries an ISO timestamp in its header and regenerates hourly, an open cell's round
# advances every round the grid runs, and the round file is spelled as an absolute path, so
# a digest over any of the three could only ever fail. `admits.json` carries no digest of
# the finished set at all, its population being the proteins with an unconstrained front.
# Each cache names its members, because a count cannot report a one-in-one-out swap.
#
# The figure's bytes are matplotlib's, with the PDF's CreationDate and the PNG's Software
# stamp suppressed and every jitter seeded per panel, so they match on a host with the same
# matplotlib as requirements.lock. The layout is measured off the drawn figure, so the
# script fixes figure.dpi and refuses a tight save box; both are part of the geometry and
# not the host's to choose. Verified byte-identical over a cold rebuild.
#
# These digests are over the finished set of 2026-11-02: 45 proteins closed on F1-F3, and
# 85 of the corpus for the per-motif counts, both named in the caches. The 85 is
# inputs/e2/corpus.json, which the composite plate's data step derives for itself
# from E1's sweep and asserts equal, so the two cannot drift; three of its members
# have no unconstrained front in E2's own screen and are read from E1's auxiliary
# tree, where the sequence the scan needs lives. The
# 45 are the finished set less eGFP and RBD, the two sequences in it that are not human
# proteins, which `cellset` excludes at every rung and names with the reason. The set moves
# as the grid closes cells, so a rebuild after an arrival will differ here and the pin is
# re-cut with the population it describes.
#
# One of the 45, Q96NI6, has an unconstrained front E2 imported from E1 rather than ran, so
# it carries points and no timing. Its wall and memory ratios are formed against the E1 run
# the front came from -- a different build on a loaded host -- which
# inputs/e2/f0_timings_imported.json states, `cost.json` names under
# `imported_unconstrained_timings`, and every row it affects carries as `f0_timing`.
